  "change_notes": {
    "source": "DOCS/CHANGELOG.md",
    "present": true,
    "heading": "v1.35.81558 — 2026-08-16",
    "highlights": [
      "Corrupt `#` heading lines no longer leak into the displayed text of 85 sections (the sprinkling rites now open directly with their antiphon).",
      "Rubrics (the red stage directions) always break onto their own line instead of running into the spoken text.",
      "Map station labels are the short liturgical names — Kyrie, Gloria, Oratio, Lectio — not essay-length titles.",
      "The map is now the Mass Map on every user surface, and a new 🔖 Annotations view indexes every highlight and margin note with jump-back-to-text, note editing, and colors.",
      "Sections carrying your annotations end with a titled ANNOTATIONS list instead of anonymous boxes.",
      "Selecting text moves a whole word at a time; shared passages open as a souvenir-plaque landing page with store badges."
    ],
    "markdown": "The reading experience matures: cleaner text, shorter map labels, and your annotations gain an index.\n\n- Corrupt `#` heading lines no longer leak into the displayed text of 85 sections (the sprinkling rites now open directly with their antiphon).\n- Rubrics (the red stage directions) always break onto their own line instead of running into the spoken text.\n- Map station labels are the short liturgical names — Kyrie, Gloria, Oratio, Lectio — not essay-length titles.\n- The map is now the Mass Map on every user surface, and a new 🔖 Annotations view indexes every highlight and margin note with jump-back-to-text, note editing, and colors.\n- Sections carrying your annotations end with a titled ANNOTATIONS list instead of anonymous boxes.\n- Selecting text moves a whole word at a time; shared passages open as a souvenir-plaque landing page with store badges."
  },
